explanation_english:
Just as ignorance makes one suffer in 'samsara', i.e. in the cycle of continuous birth and death, so knowledge has the power to free one from material bondage. Such knowledge is always accompanied by devotion to God. This sloka makes a very strong word experiment to indicate the meditation of the Absolute God.

Tat-buddayah means mind directed towards God. Tatatmanah means heart (mind, intellect) engaged only in God; Tannistha means with complete faith in God; Tatparayanah means striving that God is the ultimate goal and refuge;

Thus, the sign of true knowledge is that it leads to love of God. Because of this kind of love, devotees visit Him everywhere.
